# Shell scripts must keep LF endings in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# The team clones on Windows VDIs where `core.autocrlf` is typically `true`, which rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. Git Bash tolerates CRLF in a script — the current hook was tested
# with CRLF endings and behaves correctly — but bash on macOS/Linux does not, and a future edit
# introducing a CRLF-sensitive construct would fail silently on someone else's machine.
#
# Pinning this now costs nothing and removes a class of "works for me" bug from hooks.
*.sh text eol=lf
